[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 475,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 432,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67958,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 432,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Synovial sarcoma (SS) is a monomorphic spindle cell sarcoma with variable epithelial differentiation and a specific <em>SS18</em>-SSX fusion gene.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 476,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 433,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67959,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9040/3 Synovial sarcoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67960,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2B5A.Y &amp; XH9B22 Synovial sarcoma, other specified primary site &amp; Synovial sarcoma, NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67961,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67962,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "<p>Synovial sarcoma, monophasic spindle cell; synovial sarcoma, biphasic; synovial sarcoma, poorly differentiated</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-11T10:43:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67963,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Primary intrathoracic SS is uncommon. More than 80% of intrathoracic SSs affect pleura or pulmonary parenchyma. Mediastinum and heart are rarer primary sites {15725802; 23647858; 27401493; 29543673}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67964,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients usually present with chest pain, dyspnoea, cough, and haemoptysis. Some tumours are detected incidentally.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67965,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Primary intrathoracic SS has a slight male predilection and affects all ages, with a peak in the fourth to fifth decades of life {15725802; 17464314; 23647858; 29543673}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67966,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "<p>Unknown</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-11T10:43:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67967,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "<p>SS bears a unique chromosomal translocation that results in the formation of an oncogenic <em>SS18</em>-SSX fusion gene {29100075}. SS18-SSX protein exerts oncogenic activity by disrupting epigenetic control {29502955; 29861296}. For additional details, see the <em>Soft tissue and bone tumours</em> volume of this series [[WHO Classification of Tumours Editorial Board. Soft tissue and bone tumours. Lyon (France): International Agency for Research on Cancer; 2020. (WHO classification of tumours series, 5th ed.; vol. 3). https://publications.iarc.fr/588.]].</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-11T10:44:09"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67968,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Intrathoracic SS usually forms a large, well-circumscribed tumour. Cystic change, calcification, and necrosis may be present.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67969,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Monophasic SS consists of dense fascicles of monomorphic spindle cells with a high N:C&nbsp;ratio; entrapped pneumocytes may mislead the diagnosis or determination of subtype. Biphasic SS has epithelial and spindle cell components, in varying proportions. Poorly differentiated SS with spindle or round cell morphology shows increased cellularity, greater nuclear atypia, and high mitotic activity {9888710}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Most SSs express EMA and/or cytokeratin {15725802}. TLE1 staining is characteristic {17255769}, although it is not specific {20857142; 19363472; 30170702}. Expression of calretinin is common {11342772; 17464314}. CD56 expression {17464314}, rarely with focal synaptophysin {26136920}, may lead to misdiagnosis as small cell carcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67970,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>For FNA, a cell block preparation is favoured.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67971,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>SS18</em>-SSX fusion testing is recommended when histology and immunohistochemistry are insufficient to establish a diagnosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67972,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Monomorphic spindle cells showing variable epithelial differentiation</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Demonstration of <em>SS18</em>-SSX fusion</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67973,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) or Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM system may be used.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67974,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 210,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Intrathoracic SS is associated with poorer outcome than soft tissue SS {11905413; 15725802; 17464314; 26313782; 27401493}. In general, prognostic factors include stage, size, grade, and poorly differentiated histology {9888710; 10375108; 15364967; 18997619; 20716627}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T17:09:00"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]